            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0482" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–1044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-10T14:00:00+07:00">July 10, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 10—9:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1189. Press correspondents have reportedly returned from their visit to Yenan and
                    are en route to Chungking. We have not as yet received from the United States
                    any copies of the press despatches or articles written by them, and accordingly
                    do not know whether it has been possible for them to make comprehensive factual
                    reports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
